# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor originals — large, proprietary, re-obtainable from the vendor.
#
# The whole directory is excluded.  RE Docs/ used to live inside it, which
# forced the two binaries to be excluded by name; it now sits at the repo
# root, so the directory holds nothing but the two originals.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/iScout Mechanic-Ti VisualPlatformSetUp v3.0.6+windows/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference material kept beside the repo for cross-checking, not work
# product.  Thermal-Camera-Redux/ is a third-party app (11 MB) used to confirm
# what the device is expected to do; MechaniscoutPcap/ is 1.1 GB of USB
# captures taken while reverse-engineering the protocol.  Both are inputs to
# the RE work, so they are excluded rather than tracked — the captures in
# particular are far too large for a git history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Thermal-Camera-Redux/
/MechaniscoutPcap/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RE Workspace — derived trees, extracted or decompiled from the vendor
# binaries.  All of it is regenerated by the scripts in RE Workspace/tools/
# and RE Workspace/ghidra/, which ARE tracked.  See RE Docs 02.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/RE Workspace/apk/
/RE Workspace/exe/
/RE Workspace/jadx/
/RE Workspace/logs/
/RE Workspace/ghidra/out/
/RE Workspace/ghidra/proj/
/RE Workspace/ghidra/win/
__pycache__/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/linux-port/build/

# Differential harness: compiled shim libraries, harness/probe binaries, and
# the patched copy of the vendor .so.
/linux-port/tools/thermometry_diff/build/

# Shared bionic shim (tools/vendor_shim/) and the DYT container differential
# (tools/dytjpeg_diff/).  Both are opt-in and produce their own build trees:
# compiled shims, the prepared vendor .so, the harness binary, and the
# containers each run writes.  None of it is source.
/linux-port/tools/vendor_shim/build/
/linux-port/tools/dytjpeg_diff/build/
/linux-port/tools/dytjpeg_diff/out/
/linux-port/tools/dytjpeg_diff/out_*/

# MNN differential (tools/mnn_diff/).  Only the build tree is ignored; unlike
# dytjpeg_diff, its out/ IS tracked, because it holds the frozen vendor ground
# truth that `make check` compares the port's upscale against — in_plane.raw,
# vendor_out.raw, meta.txt and vendor.log.  Same convention as
# thermometry_diff/out/ below.
/linux-port/tools/mnn_diff/build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MNN — the optional super-resolution runtime (see linux-port/third_party/
# README.md for the recipe).  None of this is source, and all of it is large:
# MNN-src is the upstream tree, MNN-build the CMake tree, mnn-install the
# prefix the Makefile links against.  MNN_ROOT points at mnn-install, and the
# Makefile treats the runtime as genuinely optional, so a clone without any of
# this still builds and passes `make check` (via the refusing seam in
# src/mnn.c).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/linux-port/third_party/MNN-src/
/linux-port/third_party/MNN-build/
/linux-port/third_party/mnn-install/

# The port's own output.  `make check` rewrites dumpframe_*.bin on every run,
# so tracking them would leave the repo permanently dirty.  The frozen vendor
# ground truth that sits beside them — in_frame.bin, in_lut_in.bin,
# out_image.bin, meta.txt, vendor.log — is tracked: that is what --check
# compares against.
/linux-port/tools/thermometry_diff/out/*/dumpframe_lut.bin
/linux-port/tools/thermometry_diff/out/*/dumpframe_out.bin
/linux-port/tools/thermometry_diff/out/*/port_lut.bin
/linux-port/tools/thermometry_diff/out/*/port_out.bin

# Viewer snapshots.  dytview's `s` key writes a timestamped PNG
# (dytview_YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS.png) into the *current working directory*, so
# launching it from the repo root would otherwise leave an untracked image
# beside the sources.  Deliberately not anchored to a directory: the snapshot
# lands wherever dytview was started from.
dytview_*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored libuvc
#
# The sources are tracked directly rather than as a submodule, because the
# build needs include/libuvc/libuvc_config.h — hand-written here to replace
# the header CMake would generate, and therefore absent from upstream.  A
# gitlink would drop it and break the build.
#
# The original shallow clone's .git (tag v0.0.8, commit 4e9fc77) was moved
# aside rather than deleted.  It is provenance only; upstream is re-clonable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/linux-port/third_party/libuvc/.git-upstream-backup/
